$DIR/main.p:13:10: p was moved to the task started by task p.Serve() at line 12, so it can no longer be used here
    owned[Server] is an owner type: its values own what they hold and release it
    when they are dropped. Starting a method of an owned box with a task
    statement moves the box into the new task, which drops it when the method
    returns, instead of copying it, so that what it owns has exactly one owner.
    Since line 12, p holds nothing.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    To keep using p while the task runs, make it a synced box: the task then
    takes a reference of its own:
        p := alloc.Synced[Server]()
    If this is the last use of p, move it before line 12, where p still holds
    its value.
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3301" for a longer explanation)
